{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45410-demons-in-the-past","id":45410,"title":"Demons in the Past","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-08T23:19:51-08:00","id":45410,"title":"Demons in the Past","content":"(There's another thread on a similar topic, but this one has enough of a different thrust that I feel it's worth starting a new one.)<br /> <br /> So, <i>Demon: the Descent</i> has a heavy focus on its technological trappings, creating a spectacular effect. The idea of unique robotic monster hiding inside human-skin suits is freaking amazing, and I hope to play the ever-loving crap out of it.<br /> <br /> However, I must admit that I'm curious about what demons looked like in the past. As far as I can tell, both <i>Demon</i> and the GMC book are vague about the history of the God-Machine and how high-tech its designs were (which I appreciate--no need to overload the players with history that doesn't affect the present-day story at all). Whether the God-Machine and its creations have always looked the way they do now and we're only just catching up to the mechanical and cybernetic components of the Machine, or the Machine upgrades itself over time using the latest human technology, seems a little unclear and is probably left to the GM to decide.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I find myself enamored by the idea of older demons being somewhat more archaic in design. Constructs of wood and rope powered by torsion, brass-helmeted clockwork Antikythera demons, clanking whistling demons of brass and steam. I like imagining what such a creature would look like using the technology of the past, and how it might transform itself into a mishmash of bizarre anachronism over time as it adds modern night-vision lenses to its aging brass face.<br /> <br /> Of course, that even suggests that the God-Machine and its angels (and thus, its demons) are even old enough for this to be a viable thing. Like I said, so far as I can tell, the book doesn't say anything about that. What do people think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","name":"Deflare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T00:33:07-08:00","id":45427,"title":"","content":"My understanding (based on the reading of the Chronicle parts of the God Machine book) is that the GM's cover is what appears as relevant to the era, while hiding the technology underneath it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it certainly suggests that more archaic designs are certainly possible, be it wooden built angels or other fancy stuff like Steampunk Demons made up of bogglingly complex series of valves and compressors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T01:35:32-08:00","id":45441,"title":"","content":"In my own medieval chronicles I took the hiding aspect with latest human technology mostly for infrastructure. Thus a mill (gears? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) could be part of infrastructure, or secret passways inside a castle (here even more modern gears could be and modern technologies).<br /> <br /> For angels I didnt tech them down but gave them more appearances that looked like those in the lore of that time. For example one who was quite big and could spit acid: A dragon who spits &quot;flames&quot; (acid) that melts things. Only thing is in moonlight his scales are glinting strangely as if they are made out of pure metal. And wires inside look like metallic ropes to teh medieval onlooker,...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T11:34:12-08:00","id":45733,"title":"","content":"Purely in practical terms, the God Machine pilfers resources that are available from the age it exists within... so in more ancient times, it would be using chariot wheels instead of manhole covers, and wood instead of steel, only because those materials were more abundant in order to craft itself / it's angels from. It would adapt as time went on with superlative intellect, not really diminishing itself considerably, and perhaps even expanding - has humanity mastered steel and fire because IT wishes to, or because the God Machine needs digital watches to construct a particular matrix in 2042 and we're just a footnote to that plan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T14:44:14-08:00","id":45854,"title":"","content":"This really does depend on the storyteller's fiat with the Machine. For example, my PCs have the theory that the GM was built in the future, and is using time travel to retroactively conquer the universe and pull it into its design from the very beginning. thus, while the language and resources for Infrastructure are archaic and dated, it appears no more or less techy than it does in the modern times. Only demons really become part of the era, in that mindset. the Machine and its angels are outsiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T18:34:11-08:00","id":45978,"title":"","content":"...I can't wait til Dark Eras comes out with a 'past' Demon setting. It'll help answer all these questions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T19:31:02-08:00","id":46002,"title":"","content":"Clockwork. Clockwork everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T19:15:08-08:00","id":47190,"title":"","content":"Wondering how would the aether stuff work in a setting where there's no mechanical things running yet. (Storing Aether, specifically)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T06:47:56-08:00","id":47356,"title":"","content":"As long as there are clocks, it works. <br /> <br /> Now if there are no clocks, demons gonna be a bit screwed on that front. Still, you might find them doing stuff like storing it in water mills or replicating Hero of Alexandria's steam engine (or stealing one of his originals).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T07:33:24-08:00","id":47373,"title":"","content":"I adhere to the theory that the God Machine only uses currently available technologies (and close occult relatives) for itself and its angels. It pushes mankind to develop some new technologies so it can use it. This would mean that in the past the God Machine and its angels were less complex en maybe less strong. I do have a hard time conceptualizing a machine from the time before clockwork. Maybe it only consisted of occult matrices during that time and only incorporated the machine parts later for greater efficiency?<br /> <br /> But as the Antikythera mechanism is from around 100 BC, you have to go more than 2100 years in the past before clockwork becomes inprobable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T10:30:09-08:00","id":47460,"title":"","content":"The great machines of the Classical era were pumps, triremes, and siege engines (that's why I was postulating demons of wood and torsion--they're based on catapults). People are clever, and have been coming up with clever ways to do things for millenia. I wonder if there might have been more muscle-power involved in the early God-Machine's Infrastructure, with cultists ritually turning the cranks of its first gears.<br /> <br /> If you want clocks specifically, besides astronomically-significant stone arrangements like Stonehenge, water clocks are attested in the West since the 1500s BCE, and from what I can tell, they were pretty sophisticated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","name":"Deflare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:22:18-08:00","id":47731,"title":"","content":"Mankind has long kept to the idea of &quot;storing power&quot; far longer then to the idea of clockworks and gears.<br /> <br /> Remember that the God-Machine exists in multiple realms and multiple quantum states simultaneously. That includes the Astral Realm and Shadow, both of which have a bidirectional relationship with the Fallen World. As long as an idea is in the human mindset, it's echoed in the Temenos, and as long as an event or object has significance, it too has its echo in the Shadow. As shamans kept medicine bags and totems to store power, so too could the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> This is just a prolonged and attempt-at-based-in-canon reason to say that as long as there have been objects of power, the God-Machine and its servants have been using them to enact the G-M's will in the world. Pretty much watch any episode of Ancient Aliens for inspiration of Infrastructure in ancient times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T16:50:27-08:00","id":48581,"title":"","content":"Surface-level infrastructure can change, but I like to imagine demonic and angelic forms as following from the same esoteric technologies. Less steampunk and more Cowboys v Aliens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}